<title>PERU: Peru's October cotton output rises 91 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's October cotton output rises 91 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's October cotton production rose 91 percent to 11,225 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Thursday.</p>
<p>Output in the first ten months rose to 255,883 tonnes from 211,439 tonnes in the same period in 1995, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 216,869 tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of cotton in October fell 49.8 percent to $2.090 million, while imports in the first ten months dropped 49.0 percent to $18.166 million.</p>
<p>Exports of cotton in October fell 26.5 percent to $2.783 million, but exports in the first ten months rosed 68.2 percent to $23.273 million.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
